वह्नि, इस्, इस्, इ, bearing, carrying, bringing (Ved.);
luminous, bright (Ved.); (इस्), m. one who bears an
oblation (to the gods), a sacrificer, priest (Ved.);
‘borne along,’ an epithet of the Maruts (Ved.); of
Soma (Ved.); of the gods in general (Ved.); fire
(= Agni); a horse (Naigh.

वह्य-शीवन्, आ, अरी, अ, or वह्ये-शय, अस्, आ,
अम्, Ved. lying in a palanquin; reclining on a couch;
[cf. तल्प-शीवन्.]
